'''Scosglen''' is a massive rift accessible by killing [[Bul-Kathos]] in the [[Arreat Summit (past)|Assault on Mount Arreat]].

==Lore==
During Uileloscadh Mór, the assault of forces of Hell on Mount Arreat, Druids in the forests of Scosglen came under attack. Like their Barbarian brethren, they have sworn to protect the powerful mysteries below the peaks, lest all humanity suffer greatly. Help them defend their homeland and thwart Baal's forces from corrupting and destroying everything.

==Drop bias==
Increased chance to drop Enhanced Runes, sacred base items, and special [[Cube Reagents|oils]] (of Conjuration, Greater Luck, Augmentation, and Intensity).

Etherborns always drop at least rare quality items and have a chance to drop entire Arcane Crystals.

[[Sapling Guard]]s have the highest chances to drop one or several runes.

==Other Loot==
You can find four [[Protected Chest]]s in Scosglen, each dropping a scroll. Four can be combined to make an Item Design for the charm [[Charms#Dúlra_Aegis|Dúlra_Aegis]]. 

Corrupted Druids drop a [[Corrupted Treasure]] on death. They also have a chance to drop an Item Design (Tenet) or a completed Tenet specific to the druid type. 

Near the top-right of the map is a boss, [[Eleveth Eye]], which can drop corrupted shards and a Reality Piercer. When cubed with the Dúlra Aegis in Túr Dúlra, this will open a portal to The Frozen Crest, whose boss Sescheron's Destroyer drops the final component to upgrade the Dúlra Aegis.

